-- title:
--   Function field of the base change to ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a commutative ring equipped with a $\mathbb Q$-algebra structure, and let $\pi_X : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R_0$ be a morphism of schemes with $X$ integral and with the pullback $X' = X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R_0} \operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb Q}$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` also integral; assume that $R_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is injective. Let $F$ be a field which is a $\mathbb Q$-algebra together with a ring isomorphism $e_F : F \xrightarrow{\sim} K(X)$ onto the function field of $X$ (the stalk of $\mathcal O_X$ at the generic point), let $\bar F$ be a field which is a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra, and let $\mathrm{toBar} : F \to \bar F$ be a ring homomorphism such that: $\mathrm{toBar}$ is compatible with $\mathbb Q \to F$ and $\mathbb Q \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$; the subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with the image of $\mathrm{toBar}$ is all of $\bar F$; and for every finite subset $s \subseteq F$ which is $\mathbb Q$-linearly independent, its image under $\mathrm{toBar}$ is $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linearly independent. Assume finally that $e_F^{-1}$ carries the composite $R_0 \to \Gamma(X, X) \to K(X)$ (global sections pulled back along $\pi_X$, then the germ at the generic point) to $R_0 \to \mathbb Q \to F$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $e_{\bar F} : \bar F \xrightarrow{\sim} K(X')$ such that, first, for every $z \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, $e_{\bar F}$ sends the image of $z$ in $\bar F$ to `baseToFunctionField` of the second projection applied to $z$, that is to the germ at the generic point of $X'$ of the pullback of $z$ under $\operatorname{pr}_2 : X' \to \operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and second, for every open $U \subseteq X$ with $U$ non-empty and with its preimage under the first projection $\operatorname{pr}_1 : X' \to X$ non-empty, and every $t \in \Gamma(X, U)$, $e_{\bar F}(\mathrm{toBar}(e_F^{-1}(\text{germ of } t \text{ in } K(X))))$ is the germ in $K(X')$ of the pullback $\operatorname{pr}_1^{*}t \in \Gamma(X', \operatorname{pr}_1^{-1}U)$.
--
--   This identifies $\bar F$, presented abstractly as the constant field extension of $F \cong K(X)$ by $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (generation plus linear disjointness over $\mathbb Q$), with the function field of the base change $X_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$, compatibly with constants and with germs of local sections. It is used in the construction of a curve model for the geometric function field of a Shimura curve model, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.ShimuraCurveModel.ModuliWitnessD.exists_curveModel_iso_gal_baseChange`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.ShimuraCurveModel.ModuliWitnessD.exists_curveModel_iso_gal_baseChange).
